The capture script auto-clicks a button with text "Start" / "Play" (exact match, case insensitive). I'll make the start button text "START" and aria-label "Start". But if there are multiple eligible buttons, it becomes ambiguous. Other buttons on the start screen (sound, tilt, quality) should not have start/play labels. So the primary CTA "START ENGINE" won't match regex; it must be exactly "Start" or "Play" (or "Start Game"/"Play Now"). If the button contains extra text (e.g., "START ENGINE →"), it won't auto-click. Better: primary button text exactly "START" and a small sub-label outside the button. Then auto-capture works. But capture will click start and screenshot after 1s — countdown may show. For the final capture that's fine (it will show game). For my own screenshots I'll use custom playwright scripts with direct evaluate to start instantly.

